# Code owners. Available on public repositories with GitHub Free.
#
# Pair this with a ruleset that requires review from Code Owners and these
# become mandatory reviewers rather than a suggestion.
#
# Every path names BOTH of you. Nobody can approve their own pull request, so a
# path owned by one person alone could never merge a change that person wrote.
# An owner without write access to the repository is silently ignored.

# Default: either of you.
*                                @ez4hecker @ruatahmar

# The three places where a mistake is either invisible or unrepairable.
# CONTRIBUTING.md already says review is not optional here; this enforces it.
# The default line already covers them; they are listed so the reason is
# recorded next to the path, and so they survive a change to the default.

# ADR 0046's rules are frozen from the first written row. A change here
# orphans every existing suppression digest, silently and permanently.
/packages/crypto/                @ez4hecker @ruatahmar

# withOrg(), the three roles, the RLS policies. Every later ticket assumes
# this is right (E0-2).
/packages/db/                    @ez4hecker @ruatahmar

# An applied migration is not editable. A wrong one is a production incident.
/packages/db/migrations/         @ez4hecker @ruatahmar

# ADR 0054: a decision is never edited in place. Superseding one should be a
# conversation, not a commit.
/docs/adr/                       @ez4hecker @ruatahmar

# The gates. Weakening one should be as visible as the rule it enforces.
/scripts/                        @ez4hecker @ruatahmar
